                                "sense_id": "5f1152b4-5ec4-3c8f-8c96-24e6b42cf913",
                                "text": "A little while later, when I came to the dining-room for the first breakfast, I met Lovaina in a blue-figured aahu of muslin and lace, a close-fitting, sweeping nightgown, the single garment that Tahitians wear all day and take off at night, a tunic, or Mother Hubbard, which reveals their figures without disguise, unstayed, unpetticoated."
                            }
